================================================================================

Capsule links third-party components. The list below records every dependency
whose license carries an attribution, notice, or source-availability obligation
that Capsule must discharge when it distributes a binary, plus the license
elections Capsule makes where a dependency is offered under a choice of terms.

It is not a complete dependency inventory. Permissively licensed dependencies
whose obligations are satisfied by shipping this file (MIT, Apache-2.0,
BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, BSL-1.0, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0, 0BSD,
MIT-0, Unlicense, and the various OR-combinations of these) are not enumerated
individually; their license texts are reproducible from the dependency tree with
`cargo metadata`. The machine-checked policy that governs which licenses may
enter this tree at all is `deny.toml`, and the rationale is
capsule-docs/src/content/docs/design/licensing.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tzf-rel — Open Database License v1.0 (ODbL-1.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Capsule embeds the `tzf-rel` timezone boundary database (reached through the
MIT-licensed `tzf-rs` crate) in every distributed binary: the `capsule` CLI, the
server binaries, the iOS static library, the Android shared library, and the
WebAssembly bundle.

  Contains information from the Timezone Boundary Builder database, which is
  made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0.
  <https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/>

  Upstream database: <https://github.com/evansiroky/timezone-boundary-builder>
  Rust packaging:    <https://github.com/ringsaturn/tzf-rel>

Capsule redistributes this database unmodified and creates no Derivative
Database. The ODbL share-alike obligation attaches to the database, not to
Capsule's own source code. The unmodified database is available from the
upstream sources above under the ODbL.

