  ring          Apache-2.0 AND ISC
  aws-lc-rs     ISC AND (Apache-2.0 OR ISC)
  aws-lc-sys    ISC AND (Apache-2.0 OR ISC) AND Apache-2.0 AND MIT AND
                BSD-3-Clause AND (Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT) AND
                (Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT-0)
  brotli        BSD-3-Clause AND MIT
  encoding_rs   (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause
  matchit       MIT AND BSD-3-Clause
  unicode-ident (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License elections
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Where a dependency is offered under a choice of licenses, Capsule elects a
permissive term. One election is worth recording explicitly:

  r-efi   Offered as `MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later`. Capsule elects
          MIT. Capsule does not accept the LGPL-2.1-or-later arm, and no
          copyleft obligation arises from this dependency. `r-efi` is reached
          only through `getrandom`/`wasi` and is compiled only for UEFI and
          wasm32 targets.

For every other multi-licensed dependency Capsule elects MIT where offered, and
otherwise the first permissive term listed in its SPDX expression.
